{
 "id": "inplace/taken-over-by-another-operator/cold-hot/5m",
 "description": "Extract shortens m9 from 8,000 to 7,000 tokens on request 1. On request 2, after the entry expired, a sweep shortens the same m9 from 8,000 to 500 tokens, and extract is no longer applied or reported. The forwarded m9 has the sweep's size: it is not the client's size, so the restore check does not end extract, and it is not extract's SizeAfter. The library must end extract (accountant#70). Only the sweep is priced, with 7,500 tokens, and no check fails. On request 3 the sweep is applied again and is the only change in the state. Before the fix extract stayed active, the sum check counted 1,000 tokens too many, and the host booked nothing for every request of the session.",
 "source": "issue_cases.md#70",
